{
  "id": "mpv",
  "name": "mpv",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "Video",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "mpv.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "io.mpv"
    ],
    "window_title": []
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://mpv.io/manual/stable/#keyboard-control"
  ],
  "note": "mpv's default bindings are documented per physical key with case treated as significant (an uppercase action requires Shift); bare letter chords below are the lowercase key, Shift+Letter chords are the uppercase key, matching the manual's own notation. Not expressible by the chord grammar, so omitted: the '*' key (increase volume; only its '0' alternate is expressible), curly-brace speed halve/double, angle-bracket playlist backward/forward, underscore cycle-video-tracks, hash cycle-audio-tracks, question-mark toggle-key-binding-overlay, the KP_DIVIDE/KP_MULTIPLY/Ctrl+KP_ADD/KP_SUBTRACT/Alt+KP_ADD/KP_SUBTRACT numpad-key alternates for volume/A-V-sync/zoom, the discouraged single-key aliases the manual itself deprecates (e for pan-and-scan, x for subtitle delay, t for move-subtitles), the MENU multimedia key, and the STOP/PREVIOUS/NEXT/ZOOMIN/ZOOMOUT multimedia keys (no equivalent in this catalog's media-key vocabulary; PREVIOUS/NEXT seek by 1 minute in mpv rather than changing tracks, so they are not mapped to previous_track/next_track). The Cmd+F fullscreen toggle and Cmd+0/1/2 window-resize chords are macOS-only per the manual but no separate mac bindings are given for the rest of the list since the manual documents one shared, platform-independent set.",
